<PageLayout
  title="Our Vision"
  eyebrow="Why we exist"
  intro="Healing hearts, renewing communities, restoring a nation. It starts with one person, opened to God."
>
  <article class="prose-page measure">
    <h2 class="!mt-0">The heart remembers</h2>
    <p>We all carry memories that still hurt. Faith doesn’t ask us to forget them. It asks us to bring them to God, who was there, and whose mercy is bigger than our pain. This is the healing of memories.</p>

    <h2>Three movements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Remembering:</strong> naming what happened, honestly.</li>
      <li><strong>Healing:</strong> bringing it to God in prayer.</li>
      <li><strong>Arising:</strong> hope, forgiveness and a new start.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>From one heart to a nation</h2>
    <p>Families and communities carry wounds too. Iva’s research in Northern Ireland explored how healing and hope can spread from one person to many.</p>
    <blockquote>Renewal begins in the heart. It doesn’t have to end there.</blockquote>

    <h2>Rooted in Ireland</h2>
    <p>From St Patrick on, this island has a long story of faith. The shamrock in our logo is a sign of that. Our hope looks forward.</p>

    <h2>Please note</h2>
    <p>We offer spiritual support, not medical or psychological treatment. We are Catholic, and everyone is welcome.</p>

